      "audited_reference": "ChromaDB addresses the challenge of distance score comparison with Neo4j by utilizing Reciprocal Rank Fusion (RRF), which merges results by rank rather than score. This method allows for effective comparison and ranking of items across both retrieval systems, as it ranks items highly only if they perform well in both systems, thereby reducing noise in the results.",
      "benchmark_id": "KGV1-005",
      "categories": [
        "single_hop",
        "compound"
      ],
      "change_rationale": "RRF belongs to the fusion layer, not ChromaDB, and does not directly compare raw distances.",
      "original_reference_sha256": "fc50842d62afba065f3dfd71fba16579b41fae079fb2ddde3eee5b0b44b421e6",
