      "audited_reference": "To set up the KineticGraph-Vectra environment, you need to follow several steps. First, check your prerequisites by ensuring Docker is installed and that you have at least 8GB of RAM available. Next, navigate to the project directory and create an environment file by copying the example file. It is crucial to edit this .env file to include your OpenAI API key, which is required for the application to function properly. The specific line to add is 'OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-actual-key-here'. After setting up the environment, you can build and start all containers using the command 'docker-compose up --build -d', and monitor the startup process through the logs. The successful startup is indicated by messages showing that the kinetic-api and kinetic-worker are running.",
