    {
      "audited_reference": "The verification and test strategies employed to ensure data security while processing complex data queries include container healthcheck validation and structural table ingestion tests. The container healthcheck validation ensures that the engine responds appropriately during standard validation sweeps, while the structural table ingestion test involves running ingestion on a standard sample document to validate that the output includes cleanly serialized Markdown grid outlines. Additionally, data security is maintained as processing runs locally within the enterprise boundary, ensuring that corporate files never leave the system. This approach eliminates API usage charges and removes throughput bottlenecks during large-scale document backfills, thereby contributing to the integrity of the data during ingestion.",
      "benchmark_id": "KGV1-017",
      "categories": [
        "multi_hop",
        "compound",
        "two_reference_facets"
      ],
      "change_rationale": "Local parsing does not prove the entire ingestion workflow has zero external API usage or cost.",
